<slide xmlns="https://www.larkoffice.com/sml/2.0">
  <data>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="10" width="400" height="20">
      <content textType="caption" fontSize="12" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(39,121,167,1)" wrap="false" textAlign="left">
        <p>STOP 8 / 11 - CALL THE BANK</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="30" width="848" height="34">
      <content textType="title" fontSize="24" fontFamily="Inter" bold="true" color="rgba(15,36,64,1)" wrap="false" textAlign="left">
        <p>Invoke bank: a timeout means unknown</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <line startX="56" startY="64" endX="904" endY="64">
      <border color="rgb(39, 121, 167)" width="2"/>
    </line>
    <shape type="rect" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="84" width="532" height="384">
      <fill>
        <fillColor color="rgba(247,249,251,1)"/>
      </fill>
      <border color="rgb(214, 222, 232)" width="1"/>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="72" topLeftY="100" width="504" height="352">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="11" fontFamily="Roboto Mono" color="rgba(61,74,92,1)" lineSpacing="multiple:1.32" textAlign="left">
        <p>try {</p>
        <p>  String response = restTemplate.postForObject(</p>
        <p>      bankConfig.getUrl() + "/payments",</p>
        <p>      bankRequest, String.class);</p>
        <p>  context.setBankResponse(response);</p>
        <p>} catch (RestClientException e) {</p>
        <p>  // 4xx from bank  -&gt; 502 (bad gateway)</p>
        <p>  // 5xx / timeout  -&gt; 503 (we cannot know)</p>
        <p>  throw new BankUnavailableException(e);</p>
        <p>}</p>
        <p>// timeouts: connect 2s, read 5s</p>
        <p>// no auto-retry in the hot path</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="604" topLeftY="92" width="300" height="250">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="13.5" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(61,74,92,1)" lineSpacing="multiple:1.4" textAlign="left">
        <ul>
          <li><p>A timeout is not a failure - it is unknown. We answer 503 and do not auto-retry.</p></li>
          <li><p>Bank 4xx -&gt; 502; bank 5xx / timeout -&gt; 503; translated once, at the boundary.</p></li>
          <li><p>Retry belongs to the client or a scheduler - idempotency makes it safe there.</p></li>
          <li><p>The INIT record stays INIT - the trace says "unknown", never "no".</p></li>
        </ul>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="rect" topLeftX="604" topLeftY="360" width="300" height="108">
      <fill>
        <fillColor color="rgba(232,241,247,1)"/>
      </fill>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="616" topLeftY="374" width="276" height="84">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="13" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(15,36,64,1)" lineSpacing="multiple:1.35" textAlign="left">
        <p>Why it matters: the most dangerous lie in payments is pretending "unknown" is "no".</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="856" topLeftY="510" width="48" height="18">
      <content textType="caption" fontSize="12" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(138,148,166,1)" textAlign="right" wrap="false">
        <p>14 / 24</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
  </data>
  <note>
    <content textType="body">
      <p>Stop eight is the only node that talks to the bank, and it is where the second guarantee lives. We set connect and read timeouts - because the worst outcome in payments is a request that hangs forever. When the bank answers 4xx, that means our request was wrong, so we map it to 502. When it answers 5xx or times out, the result is genuinely unknown, so we return 503 and leave the record in INIT. We deliberately do not auto-retry here: with idempotency in place, a retry is safe to do from the client or a scheduled job, not in the hot path.</p>
    </content>
  </note>
